  "integrationNidTitle": "National ID verification",
  "@integrationNidTitle": {},
  "integrationNidBody": "Would confirm a patient is who they say they are against the National ID register, so one person cannot end up with three records in three health posts. It needs a credentialed connection to the National ID Management Centre, which is granted to organisations, not to an app. Until then the app matches on phone number and name, and duplicates are resolved by hand.",
  "@integrationNidBody": {},
  "integrationHmisTitle": "HMIS / DHIS2 export",
  "@integrationHmisTitle": {},
  "integrationHmisBody": "Would send the monthly aggregate this health post already counts — ANC contacts, deliveries, immunisation doses — straight into DHIS2, instead of somebody copying it onto a paper form. It needs a DHIS2 instance, an org-unit mapping and a service account from the Ministry. Until then the dashboard counts are on the phone and the paper form is still filled in by hand.",
  "@integrationHmisBody": {},
  "integrationCouncilTitle": "Provider council verification",
  "@integrationCouncilTitle": {},
  "integrationCouncilBody": "Would check a health worker's council registration number before the invite code turns their phone into a provider device, so the QR scanner cannot be activated by somebody who is not registered. It needs an API from the Nepal Health Professional Council or the Nepal Medical Council. Until then an invite code is issued by the health post and trusted on its word.",
  "@integrationCouncilBody": {},
